### Why

Section G was added in v1.5.0 as entirely `unverified` planning-guidance: the steps were derived from a plan for issue #1513 (correlation-ID functions in `hephaestus.logging`) that was never executed. Issue #1511 then executed the same core pattern — aligning `cli/__init__.py.__all__` with `cli/utils.py.__all__` — and confirmed the following verified facts: the scope should always expand to cover the full defect class (not just named symbols); eager re-export is correct and sufficient when the source module is stdlib-only; COMPATIBILITY.md does not always need updating (only when a per-symbol table exists); the subset assertion (`set(utils.__all__) - set(cli.__all__)`) is the right pin shape; and `test_import_surface.py`/`test_automation_boundary.py` must be included in the verification set. The COMPATIBILITY.md version-stamping guidance from issue #1513 remains unverified — that guidance was not exercised by issue #1511 (which had no per-symbol table to update).

